As far as I can tell, all the Java telnet applets _are_ blocked by
(properly configured) firewalls.  It is possible to "tunnel" through
firewalls using software on the client and server machines which
disguises otherwise blocked network traffic as innocuous web page
requests, but (i) the GNU httptunnel, eg., requires Unix (or a close
approximation on a Windows machine, ie. Cygwin), on your local PC;
(ii) it doesn't work very well anyway, at least the present stable
version, not supporting HTTP authentication or multiple connections
per server; (iii) firewall administrators generally take a dim view of
attempts to subvert their security, and would probably block all
access to a tunneling nethack site if they discovered their staff
playing games on it.  At least you can browse the high score lists
etc. while you are at work (or read the spoilers, heh).

